WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Benzene reacts with bromine
only when it gets help:

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:07.660
pure bromine, plus a halogen
carrier as a catalyst.

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:12.620
Now phenol solution is shaken with orange
bromine water, at room temperature.

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.120
The orange disappears, and
a white precipitate forms.

5
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.920
No catalyst at all.

6
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.860
On the ring, three hydrogen atoms have
been swapped for bromine in one go.

7
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.640
So why does phenol react so readily,
when benzene needs help?

8
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:32.040
In this mission, you'll look closely at
phenol, and how it differs from benzene.

9
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.940
Then you'll write the equation, and calculate
the mass of white solid that forms.

10
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: explain why phenol needs
no catalyst to react with bromine.